(p/'status.json').write_text(json.dumps({'scope':'read-only publication custody and boxed JSON contract','initial_included_hashes_matched':1715,'initial_included_hashes_checked':1716,'initial_mismatch':'producer custody-map basename collision','postrepair_affected_map_entries_passed':53,'unresolved_observed_custody_mismatch':False,'aggregate_hash_links_passed':17,'canonical_targets_bound':19,'newline_normalizations':['Constructor','Add11'],'cache_candidates':66,'cache_candidates_in_tracked_or_included_scope':0,'boxed_adapter_diff':'exactly actual: Actual -> actual: Box<Actual>','static_json_contract_preserved':True,'native_boxed_checks':'excluded and pending separate root record','fresh_builds_or_tests':False},indent=2)+'\n')
(p/'overview.svg').write_text('<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="980" height="330"><rect width="980" height="330" fill="white"/><g font-family="sans-serif" fill="#172638"><text x="20" y="35" font-size="23">Publication custody and static contract audit</text><text x="25" y="85" font-size="19">Initial hashes: 1715 / 1716 — one producer-map name collision</text><text x="25" y="130" font-size="19">Scoped repair: 53 / 53 affected entries match; original mismatch retained</text><text x="25" y="175" font-size="19">Aggregate links: 17 / 17; canonical Lean targets bound: 19 / 19</text><text x="25" y="220" font-size="19">66 local cache candidates; zero in tracked or included publication set</text><text x="25" y="265" font-size="18">Box&lt;Actual&gt;: one-line storage change; static JSON shape unchanged</text><text x="25" y="310" font-size="16">No build/test execution. Live boxed-check results excluded.</text></g></svg>')
subprocess.run(['rsvg-convert','-f','pdf','-o',str(p/'figure.pdf'),str(p/'overview.svg')],check=True)
(p/'report.tex').write_text(r'''\documentclass[10pt]{article}\usepackage[margin=.7in]{geometry}\usepackage{graphicx}\begin{document}\section*{Publication custody audit}\includegraphics[width=\linewidth]{figure.pdf}
\paragraph{Custody repair} The initial pass found a producer custody-map copied under the same basename as its new publication map. Root restored the original under producer-custody-map.json and recorded the correction. All53 included entries in that affected map now match; the initial mismatch remains retained. Other initially matching entries were not rehashed after repair.

\paragraph{Canonical source bindings} All19 registered modules match retained snapshots. Constructor and Add11 use only the explicitly documented terminal-newline normalization; original reviewed bytes remain retained. This is source custody, not a new proof compilation.

\paragraph{Publication set} None of66 local compiled/render-cache candidates occurs in the1,957 narrowly enumerated tracked paths or is claimed included by a custody map. Local build caches remain present. Render source and log receipts are distinguished from compiled caches.

\paragraph{Static JSON contract} The exact change against da1464 is actual:Actual to actual:Box<Actual>. Resolved Serde forwards deserialization to Actual and wraps the result, preserving JSON fields, tags and rejection policy. Boxing changes storage/allocation. No dynamic validation is inferred; root's live boxed-request checks were excluded.

\paragraph{Artifacts} REVIEW.md preserves source analysis; status.json, custody-checks.json, canonical-bindings.json, aggregate-links.json and postrepair.json retain exact scope and receipts. No repository edits, builds, tests, cloud actions or scientific execution were performed by this audit.
\end{document}''')
x=subprocess.run(['pdflatex','-interaction=nonstopmode','-halt-on-error','report.tex'],cwd=p,capture_output=True);(p/'render.stdout').write_bytes(x.stdout);(p/'render.stderr').write_bytes(x.stderr);assert x.returncode==0
subprocess.run(['pdftoppm','-f','1','-singlefile','-scale-to','1000','-png',str(p/'report.pdf'),str(p/'preview')],check=True)
(p/'manifest.json').write_text(json.dumps({'files':{str(q.relative_to(p)):sha(q) for q in sorted(p.rglob('*')) if q.is_file() and q!=p/'manifest.json'}},indent=2)+'\n');print(sha(p/'manifest.json'))
